-- ============================================================================
-- Career Path module, part 2: authored job descriptions + required
-- competencies for every job title that appears in the real career_path
-- graph (218 of 218 in-scope job titles; 0 skipped --
-- see the migration's own follow-up note for any skips).
--
-- [استنتاج] IMPORTANT: this content was AUTHORED BY CLAUDE at the explicit
-- request of the project owner (2026-07-26 session) -- it is NOT
-- transcribed from any official SRU document. "Career path.xlsx" (the real
-- source file checked this session) contains job names, grades, and
-- qualification text only; it has no job-description prose and no
-- competency-to-job-title mapping anywhere. Descriptions are templated by
-- job category (leadership/admin/technical/labor) + job family + grade;
-- required competencies are a deliberate, reviewable heuristic mapping
-- (see generate_career_path_content.js, not committed -- scratch tooling)
-- combining the 3 universal institutional competencies (communication,
-- teamwork, task/project management) with category- and family-specific
-- ones from the existing 27-competency framework, at a behavioral level
-- derived from grade (basic/practitioner/advanced/professional for grades
-- 1-4/5-8/9-12/13-16 respectively, matching CLAUDE.md's own level
-- semantics). Every row here is fully editable via the new
-- /career-path/job-titles/[id] management screen -- this is a reasonable
-- starting point for HR to review and correct, not a claimed source of
-- truth.
-- ============================================================================

